WEBVTT

00:00.525 --> 00:03.683
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.783 --> 00:07.053
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.088 --> 00:10.626
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.661 --> 00:13.631
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.666 --> 00:17.137
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.173 --> 00:20.444
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.479 --> 00:22.013
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.048 --> 00:23.382
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.417 --> 00:24.804
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.339 --> 00:37.208
Well, Chris, looks
like another day

00:37.243 --> 00:39.177
of nobody joining
us for lunch.

00:39.213 --> 00:40.580
Yeah, we never
should've let

00:40.615 --> 00:42.884
that blind girl
touch our faces.

00:44.455 --> 00:46.824
Attention, students.
This is Principal Shepherd

00:46.860 --> 00:48.894
with the lunchtime
announcements.

00:48.929 --> 00:50.898
And as a special treat,
I thought I'd deliver them

00:50.933 --> 00:54.338
in the rapping style you kids
are so enthused about.

00:54.373 --> 00:56.842
♪ Later today you're gonna
have a big thrill ♪

00:56.878 --> 00:59.514
♪ 'Cause shortly after lunch
there'll be a fire drill ♪

00:59.549 --> 01:01.785
♪ And when you go out
to wait for the bus ♪

01:01.820 --> 01:04.456
♪ Mm, go in orderly fashion,
or your hair will get mussed. ♪

01:04.491 --> 01:05.458
You suck.

01:05.493 --> 01:07.127
<i>No, you suck.</i>

01:07.163 --> 01:09.098
I can't hear you, I just presume

01:09.133 --> 01:10.534
somebody must have yelled
"You suck."

01:10.569 --> 01:12.370
Anyway, last announcement:

01:12.405 --> 01:15.609
Don't forget it's time to vote
for homecoming king and queen.

01:15.645 --> 01:18.114
Nominations are due
by 3:00 p.m. today.

01:18.149 --> 01:19.283
Peace out.

01:19.318 --> 01:22.121
<i>No, you're a douche bag.</i>

01:22.156 --> 01:25.828
Wow. Can you imagine if one
of us was homecoming king?

01:25.863 --> 01:27.998
Then people would want
to sit with us at lunch.

01:28.034 --> 01:29.836
Yeah, you should run.

01:29.871 --> 01:31.003
I'll nominate you.

01:31.039 --> 01:33.409
You know what?
I'll do it.

01:33.444 --> 01:35.110
Maybe I'll surprise everyone,

01:35.146 --> 01:37.181
like when you find out
a buttoned-up librarian

01:37.217 --> 01:39.452
is actually super sexy.

01:39.487 --> 01:41.255
Excuse me, ma'am?

01:45.867 --> 01:47.199
♪ Hot blooded... ♪

01:47.235 --> 01:48.870
Yes?

01:48.905 --> 01:52.076
There's a dead homeless man
blocking the card catalog.

01:55.516 --> 01:58.119
Well, there goes Jerome,

01:58.154 --> 02:00.022
loading the urinal up with ice.

02:00.057 --> 02:03.061
Gonna go play me
my melting game.

02:03.097 --> 02:04.397
Man, I'm starting to get drunk.

02:04.432 --> 02:05.666
Is it even noon yet?

02:05.701 --> 02:07.970
Uh, it's only 10:40.
10:40?

02:08.006 --> 02:09.239
Ah, crap,
we gotta get out of here.

02:09.275 --> 02:10.575
That's when Taco Bell throws all

02:10.610 --> 02:12.411
the breakfast food
in the Dumpster.

02:12.446 --> 02:14.081
Can't let that raccoon
get all of it.

02:14.117 --> 02:15.250
Ooh, man, you're right.

02:15.286 --> 02:16.418
You know,
this is great, guys.

02:16.453 --> 02:18.055
Drinking and
eating garbage.

02:18.090 --> 02:20.426
I'm glad we all took
a mental health day.

02:21.563 --> 02:23.332
Hey, where'd everybody go?

02:23.367 --> 02:24.667
I don't know where they went,

02:24.702 --> 02:26.704
but someone's got
to pay this check.

02:26.739 --> 02:29.677
Damn it. They left without me,
and now I'm stuck with the bill?

02:29.712 --> 02:32.682
Man, who do those guys think
I am, Mark Zuckerbrothers?

02:32.717 --> 02:34.551
Seems like they
do that a lot.

02:34.586 --> 02:36.588
Tell you what,
this one's on me.

02:36.624 --> 02:37.756
Thanks, Jerome.

02:37.792 --> 02:38.859
Since there's
no one here,

02:38.895 --> 02:40.429
do you mind
turning the TV up?

02:40.464 --> 02:43.434
That little Lamisil guy
always makes me laugh.

02:43.469 --> 02:45.771
Yeah.

02:49.313 --> 02:50.947
What do you think he is,
like a Martian?

02:50.984 --> 02:52.316
Like a little
shoe Martian?

02:52.352 --> 02:53.652
I don't know.

02:53.687 --> 02:55.889
I just hope he ain't
down there in my shoes.

02:55.925 --> 02:57.226
No, he's loud.

02:57.261 --> 02:59.596
If he were down there,
we'd know it.

02:59.631 --> 03:02.334
I ain't got
no toenails nohow.

03:06.310 --> 03:08.746
Hey, everybody,
guess what.

03:08.781 --> 03:11.318
I'm running for
homecoming king!

03:11.353 --> 03:12.353
You're what?

03:12.388 --> 03:13.989
Yeah. Neil nominated me.

03:14.025 --> 03:16.260
Why are you home
from school and Meg's not?

03:16.295 --> 03:17.929
Has she taken a lover?

03:17.965 --> 03:20.701
Well, the voting is tomorrow,
so I've got to write my speech.

03:20.736 --> 03:24.141
Luckily, "Chris Griffin"
rhymes with "homecoming king,"

03:24.176 --> 03:26.178
so I've got my opening line.

03:27.314 --> 03:28.482
Oh, my God.

03:28.518 --> 03:30.285
Did you see how
excited he is?

03:30.320 --> 03:31.453
Yeah, isn't that great?

03:31.488 --> 03:33.057
No, it's not great.

03:33.092 --> 03:35.461
Chris is not
homecoming king material.

03:35.496 --> 03:37.197
He doesn't have a
chance of winning.

03:37.232 --> 03:38.801
We got to be at
that school tomorrow

03:38.836 --> 03:40.402
to help pick up the
pieces when he loses.

03:41.541 --> 03:42.574
Oh, my Hot Pocket!

03:43.277 --> 03:45.446
Ow, it's hot!

03:50.891 --> 03:52.591
Oh, that must be Jerome.

03:52.626 --> 03:53.861
What the hell
is Jerome doing here?

03:53.896 --> 03:55.230
We didn't order any drinks.

03:55.265 --> 03:57.167
No, he and I got plans.

03:57.203 --> 03:59.002
We're gonna go down
to Carver High School

03:59.038 --> 04:01.207
and look at that mural
of black achievement.

04:01.242 --> 04:05.247
Mm, they got a manila folder
taped over Dr. Cosby's face.

04:05.282 --> 04:07.084
What? Cleveland,
you didn't tell us

04:07.120 --> 04:08.854
you had plans with Jerome.

04:08.889 --> 04:10.357
Some things are
my business.

04:10.392 --> 04:12.695
You don't tell me when
you play with yourself.

04:12.730 --> 04:14.131
Well, if you checked
my Twitter feed,

04:14.166 --> 04:15.733
I wouldn't have to.

04:25.353 --> 04:27.287
And if you elect me,
I will be as good

04:27.322 --> 04:29.958
a homecoming king
as a touchdown.

04:31.597 --> 04:33.231
And our final nominee

04:33.267 --> 04:35.636
for homecoming king
is Chris Griffin.

04:38.309 --> 04:39.609
Thank you.

04:39.645 --> 04:41.079
I'm Chris Griffin.

04:41.115 --> 04:44.151
Webster's dictionary
defines "smegma" as

04:44.187 --> 04:46.087
"a sebaceous,
cheese-like substance

04:46.123 --> 04:48.358
around the head of the penis."

04:48.394 --> 04:50.930
But what is a "king"?

04:50.965 --> 04:52.934
Oh, God,
this is already hard to watch.

04:52.969 --> 04:56.140
<i>Like that Bourne movie where
they couldn't get Matt Damon.</i>

04:56.175 --> 04:58.710
We're facing a biochemical
attack of untold proportions.

04:58.745 --> 05:00.480
Unfortunately,
Jason Bourne is not available.

05:00.516 --> 05:02.116
Who have we got?

05:02.152 --> 05:04.321
<i>We have the sixth-billed
guy from The Avengers.</i>

05:04.356 --> 05:06.225
The arrow guy
who frowns a lot.

05:06.260 --> 05:07.459
Uh, okay.

05:07.494 --> 05:08.862
Does he look
like Bourne?

05:08.898 --> 05:10.298
Yeah, yeah.

05:10.334 --> 05:12.168
He sort of looks
like a young Popeye.

05:12.204 --> 05:14.204
Well, sounds like he's
the right guy for this.

05:14.240 --> 05:17.010
Yeah... yeah.

05:17.045 --> 05:19.014
All right, students.
The votes have been tabulated,

05:19.049 --> 05:22.253
so if you could all look up
from your phones for a minute,

05:22.288 --> 05:23.755
I'll tell you who won.

05:25.194 --> 05:27.997
Children.
A man is talking.

05:28.032 --> 05:29.366
All right, I better
head down there.

05:29.401 --> 05:30.935
I brought a bag
of marshmallows

05:30.971 --> 05:32.271
and a belt for
Chris to bite on

05:32.306 --> 05:33.907
during his meltdown.

05:33.943 --> 05:37.948
And this year's James Woods High
homecoming king is...

05:37.983 --> 05:39.384
Chris Griffin.

05:39.419 --> 05:40.953
Yay!

05:40.988 --> 05:43.792
Yay!

05:43.827 --> 05:45.260
Holy crap!

05:45.296 --> 05:47.398
I don't believe it.
Chris won!

05:47.433 --> 05:49.936
All right, now it's time
for these four poor kids

05:49.972 --> 05:52.140
to thank you for
subsidizing their lunches.

05:52.175 --> 05:53.910
Thank you.

05:53.945 --> 05:55.445
Mean it.

05:55.481 --> 05:56.782
Thank you.

05:56.817 --> 05:58.084
All right.

05:58.119 --> 05:59.420
Time for my car nap.

06:06.098 --> 06:08.054
Hey, hey, hey,
there he is!

06:08.055 --> 06:09.122
The new king!

06:09.157 --> 06:10.958
I already called
and quit my job.

06:10.993 --> 06:13.129
Peter, he doesn't get money
for being homecoming king.

06:13.164 --> 06:14.397
Does he get land?

06:14.433 --> 06:15.633
No, of course not.

06:15.668 --> 06:16.935
Does he get this joke?

06:16.971 --> 06:19.073
"Shagadelic, baby!"

06:19.108 --> 06:20.776
Austin Powers!

06:20.811 --> 06:23.313
Oh, very good.
Very good, my liege.

06:23.349 --> 06:25.417
Well, Chris, since
you're royalty now,

06:25.453 --> 06:26.652
I made your favorites.

06:26.687 --> 06:27.889
Dinner for breakfast?

06:27.924 --> 06:29.123
That's right.

06:29.159 --> 06:31.127
Pork chops
and French onion soup.

06:31.163 --> 06:32.496
Oh, boy!

06:32.532 --> 06:34.734
Well, as king,
I shall eat this breakfast

06:34.769 --> 06:37.740
<i>on a tray in front
of Wheel of Fortune.</i>

06:37.775 --> 06:40.778
I'll get the TV tray,
Your Majesty.

06:40.814 --> 06:43.149
How does nobody see what's going
on with this Chris thing?

06:43.185 --> 06:44.418
What are you talking about?

06:44.453 --> 06:45.987
Well, it's obvious.

06:46.024 --> 06:47.957
The only reason they
elected him king

06:47.992 --> 06:50.362
is because they're gonna
prank him at homecoming.

06:50.398 --> 06:52.165
Shut up, Hat.
That's my brother.

06:52.201 --> 06:53.801
They're not gonna mess with him.
He's the man.

06:53.837 --> 06:56.339
He's got real Griffin beef
in those trousers.

06:56.374 --> 06:57.875
Meg, how can you be so sure?

06:57.910 --> 06:59.612
Because this kind of stuff
happens all the time

06:59.647 --> 07:01.014
to unpopular kids.

07:01.050 --> 07:02.617
They're just trying
to embarrass him

07:02.652 --> 07:04.053
and make him look stupid.

07:04.088 --> 07:05.523
You don't really think
they're going to pull

07:05.558 --> 07:06.824
a prank on Chris,
do you?

07:06.861 --> 07:08.328
I don't know,
but if they are,

07:08.363 --> 07:10.130
we got to get down to that
school and talk 'em out of it.

07:10.166 --> 07:11.400
Good idea.

07:11.436 --> 07:12.635
And luckily,
I'm great at connecting

07:12.670 --> 07:14.172
with that generation.

07:14.207 --> 07:17.177
Like when I went on that
campout with One Direction.

07:17.212 --> 07:19.146
So they checked
into their hotel suite,

07:19.182 --> 07:21.417
but the minibar
had no sparkling water.

07:21.454 --> 07:22.720
Only still.

07:23.958 --> 07:25.358
Ah, stop. It's too scary.

07:25.393 --> 07:27.028
Oh, but that's not all.

07:27.063 --> 07:28.330
They looked
in the wardrobe

07:28.366 --> 07:30.101
and discovered
that the stylist

07:30.136 --> 07:31.904
had only brought
non-skinny jeans!

07:33.408 --> 07:35.543
Do mean like a
Levi's 513 skinny straight?

07:35.579 --> 07:37.713
No. Just regular
pants that fit normal!

07:39.219 --> 07:41.387
That's not real, right?
Those aren't real?

07:41.422 --> 07:43.124
Of course not, Louis.
It's-it's just a story.

07:43.159 --> 07:45.061
Well, I guess that means
these aren't real!

07:46.431 --> 07:48.033
Yeah, they're gonna die
in the woods.

07:48.068 --> 07:49.568
Simon, are they tagged?

07:49.604 --> 07:50.771
They're tagged, right?

07:50.806 --> 07:52.640
Oh, they're tagged.
Good.

07:52.676 --> 07:54.243
Simon, did I ever
tell you the one

07:54.278 --> 07:55.546
about the
loose-fitting T-shirt?

07:55.581 --> 07:58.484
No, no, no, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no, no...

08:02.527 --> 08:03.828
All right,
if we want Cleveland

08:03.863 --> 08:05.504
to stop spending
all his time with Jerome,

08:05.533 --> 08:06.967
<i>we got to remind him
how much fun we are.</i>

08:07.002 --> 08:08.235
So let's just have fun.

08:08.271 --> 08:09.438
How do we do that?

08:09.473 --> 08:10.640
I don't know.

08:10.675 --> 08:12.576
Little bit of this.

08:12.611 --> 08:14.313
Okay.
That seems like fun.

08:14.349 --> 08:15.916
What about one of these?

08:15.951 --> 08:17.318
Yeah, sure.
There's no wrong moves.

08:17.354 --> 08:19.288
What if I brush
my shoulders off?

08:19.324 --> 08:22.027
Original ideas
are preferred, but sure.

08:22.062 --> 08:24.798
Three fun guys,
room for four.

08:24.834 --> 08:25.967
I don't know if
it's working, Peter.

08:26.003 --> 08:27.136
I don't know
if it's fun.

08:27.171 --> 08:28.940
It's more than fun,
it's "foon."

08:28.975 --> 08:30.609
That's a fun way
to say "fun."

08:30.644 --> 08:33.314
Hey, how foon would it be
if we waved sticks around?

08:33.349 --> 08:35.218
I-I really don't know
what we're doing.

08:35.253 --> 08:36.854
It's foon,
from the word before.

08:36.889 --> 08:38.724
I don't see what's...

08:38.760 --> 08:41.529
All right, first,
let's take your blood pressure,

08:41.564 --> 08:43.032
'cause that's-that's
like our favorite thing

08:43.067 --> 08:44.834
to do around here.

08:48.376 --> 08:50.745
<i>Okay, we all know how much
Cleveland loves Tecmo Bowl,</i>

08:50.781 --> 08:52.148
so let's start playing.

08:52.183 --> 08:53.383
I'm the Raiders.
I'm Bo Jackson.

08:53.419 --> 08:54.886
And hopefully,
he'll show up.

08:54.921 --> 08:56.688
That's no fair.
Bo Jackson's too fast.

08:56.724 --> 08:58.726
Guys, do we want
Cleveland back or don't...

08:58.761 --> 08:59.928
Uhp, here we go.

08:59.964 --> 09:02.366
Bye-bye.

09:02.401 --> 09:03.602
See, Peter? He's too fast.

09:03.638 --> 09:05.004
You got to tackle me.
It's "B."

09:05.039 --> 09:06.507
You got to press "B."

09:06.543 --> 09:08.210
I'm pressing "B." He's too fast.

09:08.245 --> 09:09.779
Going over here.

09:09.815 --> 09:11.115
Going over here now.

09:11.150 --> 09:12.350
Never get tired.

09:12.386 --> 09:14.555
Change your guy, Quagmire.

09:14.590 --> 09:15.757
Change your guy.

09:15.792 --> 09:17.026
I'm trying.
Peter's cheating.

09:17.061 --> 09:18.395
You're cheating, Peter.

09:18.430 --> 09:19.630
I'm not cheating.
I'm following the rules.

09:19.666 --> 09:21.066
I'm just really good.

09:21.102 --> 09:23.404
You're not really good.
You just got Bo Jackson.

09:23.439 --> 09:26.409
Bo Jackson also played
professional baseball.

09:26.444 --> 09:28.379
Shut up, Joe.
Everybody knows that.

09:28.415 --> 09:29.582
Kansas City.

09:29.617 --> 09:30.717
Royals.

09:30.752 --> 09:32.587
Can't stop.
Won't stop.

09:32.622 --> 09:37.262
Bo... might...
go... all... the...

09:37.297 --> 09:39.099
Nope, going back
the other way.

09:39.135 --> 09:40.969
What? Are you going backwards?
Just score.

09:41.004 --> 09:42.805
Nah, I'm gonna run
out the quarter.

09:42.840 --> 09:44.942
I'm not playing now.
My controller's down.

09:44.978 --> 09:46.845
Seems like your controller's
been down the whole time.

09:46.882 --> 09:49.818
Who's Veris?
You got to switch off Veris.

09:49.853 --> 09:52.022
Get it to Ronnie Lott.

09:52.057 --> 09:54.860
Pretty much anyone
but Veris.

09:54.896 --> 09:57.632
Oh, no, I'm all the
way back here now.

09:57.667 --> 09:59.702
I'm in my own end zone.
What am I doing?

09:59.738 --> 10:01.438
Too bad I'm not
Bo Jackson.

10:01.474 --> 10:02.675
Oh, wait. I am!

10:02.710 --> 10:04.010
Ridiculous.

10:04.045 --> 10:05.780
Oh, yeah.

10:05.815 --> 10:07.216
There you go,
Quagmire.

10:07.251 --> 10:08.485
You're about
to tackle me.

10:08.520 --> 10:09.787
But then...

10:09.822 --> 10:11.823
Damn it!

10:11.859 --> 10:12.960
Less than a minute.

10:12.995 --> 10:14.295
Shut up, Joe!

10:14.330 --> 10:15.464
He's gonna do it.

10:15.500 --> 10:16.733
He might do this.

10:16.769 --> 10:17.901
I don't know, a
lot of football

10:17.937 --> 10:19.071
still to be
played here.

10:19.106 --> 10:20.339
I'm hitting reset.

10:20.374 --> 10:21.676
Don't you dare
hit reset.

10:21.711 --> 10:23.011
You hit reset, you're
banned for life.

10:23.047 --> 10:24.213
I hate this.

10:24.248 --> 10:25.683
Joe, do you want to play?

10:25.718 --> 10:27.653
Nah, I like being
this guy.

10:27.689 --> 10:30.190
A zig. A zag.
A touchdown!

10:30.226 --> 10:32.494
Yeah!

10:32.530 --> 10:33.831
♪ I won the game ♪

10:33.866 --> 10:35.434
♪ And now I'm gonna jump ♪

10:35.469 --> 10:36.868
♪ Bo Jackson! ♪

10:38.641 --> 10:40.243
All right, if we want
to get Cleveland back,

10:40.278 --> 10:42.246
we should just put out
his favorite snack:

10:42.281 --> 10:43.749
an open can of tuna.

10:43.784 --> 10:46.621
Often he'll come running
when he hears a can opening.

10:46.656 --> 10:48.290
Peter, stop.

10:48.325 --> 10:49.927
Yeah, I think it's
time we addressed

10:49.962 --> 10:51.528
the elephant
in the room.

10:51.564 --> 10:52.932
There's a simple reason

10:52.967 --> 10:55.469
Cleveland is hanging out
with Jerome and not us.

10:55.504 --> 10:57.373
Jerome is black
and we're not.

10:57.408 --> 10:58.742
Yeah, I mean,
you can't blame him.

10:58.777 --> 11:00.479
It's just a thing
they have in common.

11:00.514 --> 11:01.880
Something they can bond over.

11:01.916 --> 11:03.484
Well, I guess
that makes sense.

11:03.519 --> 11:05.621
I suppose people do want
to be with their own kind.

11:05.657 --> 11:08.626
Like the audience at a
Decemberists concert.

11:08.662 --> 11:10.462
Good evening,
white guys who weigh less

11:10.498 --> 11:12.133
than their girlfriends.

11:20.015 --> 11:21.583
God, a lot
of gym teacher

11:21.619 --> 11:23.520
suicide memorials
in this place.

11:23.555 --> 11:25.256
All right, let's find
the coolest kids here,

11:25.291 --> 11:27.360
and see if they know anything
about a prank on Chris.

11:27.395 --> 11:29.597
Those chicks in the
skirts look pretty cool.

11:29.633 --> 11:32.169
Hey there.
Brian Rockwell.

11:32.204 --> 11:33.872
This is my friend,
Stewie Goldberg.

11:33.908 --> 11:35.274
What?

11:35.309 --> 11:36.544
I don't know my way
around the school,

11:36.579 --> 11:37.678
so I figured I'd get the deets

11:37.714 --> 11:38.780
from a couple of seniors.

11:38.816 --> 11:40.017
Download me.

11:40.052 --> 11:41.618
Brian-- it's not
Goldberg, by the way--

11:41.654 --> 11:42.788
we should ask
about the prank.

11:42.824 --> 11:44.324
I'm earning their trust.

11:44.360 --> 11:45.559
Hey, uh, I'm new here,

11:45.594 --> 11:47.129
but you know what'd be crazy?

11:47.164 --> 11:48.465
If me, a guy,

11:48.500 --> 11:50.535
went in the girls' room
with you two.

11:50.571 --> 11:52.840
I mean, that would be,
that would be so wild.

11:52.875 --> 11:54.642
We should, we should
totally just go in there.

11:54.678 --> 11:55.878
Brian, stop.

11:55.913 --> 11:57.047
That'd be hilarious.

11:57.082 --> 11:58.249
I'm in.

11:58.284 --> 11:59.651
Stewie, go wait
in the car.

11:59.687 --> 12:01.489
No, we are here to get
information about Chris.

12:01.524 --> 12:03.592
I said, go wait
in the car.

12:07.100 --> 12:09.436
They had security guards
in the bathroom.

12:09.471 --> 12:12.741
We-we live in such
a culture of fear now.

12:16.817 --> 12:19.353
Hey, guys, what are
you doing here?

12:19.388 --> 12:21.090
And why are you
dressed like that?

12:21.125 --> 12:22.959
Well, we realized you like
hanging out with Jerome

12:22.995 --> 12:24.430
because he's black,

12:24.465 --> 12:27.101
so we wanted you to know
we can be black guys, too.

12:27.136 --> 12:30.107
Yeah, in fact, we can even
be famous movie black guys.

12:30.142 --> 12:31.375
I'm Bagger Vance.

12:31.410 --> 12:33.145
I also am
Bagger Vance.

12:33.181 --> 12:35.248
<i>I'm Kazaam from Kazaam.</i>

12:35.284 --> 12:36.819
You really think
I'm only hanging out

12:36.854 --> 12:38.655
with Jerome 'cause he's black?

12:38.690 --> 12:41.827
I hang out with Jerome because,
unlike some people,

12:41.862 --> 12:44.398
he actually takes
an interest in my life.

12:44.433 --> 12:46.235
And he would never
stick me with the bill

12:46.270 --> 12:48.372
by walking out
on me at the Clam.

12:50.144 --> 12:52.279
Well, we could have come over
and graciously apologized,

12:52.315 --> 12:53.849
but we took a chance.

12:53.884 --> 12:55.953
That's what I like about us.

13:00.997 --> 13:02.698
Sucks we didn't find
out what kind of prank

13:02.733 --> 13:04.034
they're gonna
pull on Chris.

13:04.070 --> 13:05.637
<i>I know that book
is The Hunger Games</i>

13:05.672 --> 13:06.972
with the cover taken off.

13:07.008 --> 13:08.775
Oh, look, something on TV.

13:08.811 --> 13:11.815
And finally, tonight, a moving
story from James Woods High,

13:11.850 --> 13:15.053
where the student body has made
their homecoming a special event

13:15.089 --> 13:17.224
for a very special boy.

13:17.260 --> 13:18.827
And this year's James Woods High

13:18.862 --> 13:22.500
homecoming king is
Chris Griffin.

13:22.536 --> 13:24.571
Yay!

13:24.606 --> 13:27.042
Yay!

13:27.077 --> 13:28.478
That's right. Chris Griffin,

13:28.513 --> 13:30.849
a tubby spaz
with a heart full of dreams,

13:30.884 --> 13:32.853
gets to feel normal for a night,

13:32.888 --> 13:35.056
thanks to the kindness
of his peers.

13:35.091 --> 13:37.894
Oh.

13:37.930 --> 13:39.264
I just see him
walking around

13:39.300 --> 13:41.067
with his hands down
his pants all day,

13:41.102 --> 13:42.870
and he's just so
fat and weird,

13:42.905 --> 13:44.607
so we feel bad.

13:44.642 --> 13:48.247
Yeah, last year we did the burnt
up kid, so this was a slam dunk.

13:48.282 --> 13:50.450
Oh, my God, they just
elected him out of pity,

13:50.485 --> 13:52.287
because they think he's
mentally challenged.

13:52.323 --> 13:54.925
Kind of like we did
with George W. Bush.

13:54.961 --> 13:57.129
Huh? Right?

13:57.165 --> 13:59.801
I-I guess.
I guess, Brian.

13:59.836 --> 14:01.236
I-I don't--
I don't know.

14:01.272 --> 14:02.833
Let's-let's just watch
some commercials.

14:07.052 --> 14:09.020
Well, that explains it.

14:09.055 --> 14:10.456
The only reason Chris
is homecoming king

14:10.492 --> 14:12.459
is that all the other
kids feel sorry for him.

14:12.495 --> 14:13.695
Do you think he knows?

14:13.730 --> 14:14.864
I can't imagine.

14:14.899 --> 14:16.099
And we can't tell him.

14:16.135 --> 14:17.402
It would destroy him.

14:20.075 --> 14:21.242
Look away!

14:21.277 --> 14:23.713
No one may meet
the king's gaze.

14:23.748 --> 14:25.216
So, uh, hey,

14:25.252 --> 14:27.386
congratulations
again on that, uh,

14:27.422 --> 14:28.789
homecoming thing.

14:28.825 --> 14:30.391
Why congratulate
me on a right

14:30.427 --> 14:32.328
and natural
turn of events?

14:32.364 --> 14:33.664
Now, if you'll
excuse me,

14:33.699 --> 14:35.134
I shall select
three things

14:35.170 --> 14:37.671
from Stewie's room
that I wish to be mine.

14:37.707 --> 14:40.176
There's a book in there
on how to eat healthy.

14:40.211 --> 14:42.346
Why don't you take that,
you fat bitch?

14:42.382 --> 14:44.784
Well, he obviously doesn't
know it's just a pity vote.

14:44.820 --> 14:46.754
In fact, this whole
homecoming king thing

14:46.789 --> 14:48.858
seems to have just gone
straight to his head.

14:48.893 --> 14:50.829
I know, he's acting like
an arrogant jerk.

14:50.864 --> 14:52.331
Quiet, Rupert!

14:52.366 --> 14:54.502
It is an honor to serve
the king in this manner.

14:54.537 --> 14:55.703
Brian, this can't go on.

14:55.738 --> 14:57.440
Chris is out of control.

14:57.476 --> 15:00.313
He's even more arrogant
than an actor/writer/director.

15:00.348 --> 15:02.984
Well, my script is brilliant,
and I'm a great director.

15:03.019 --> 15:06.757
The question is,
how bad do I want this part?

15:08.496 --> 15:10.898
Okay, I'll do it.

15:15.609 --> 15:16.741
Well, now we know.

15:16.777 --> 15:18.845
Neither of us
likes crepes.

15:18.882 --> 15:21.316
See, that's another thing
we got in common.

15:21.352 --> 15:23.387
In fact, you want
to hear something crazy?

15:23.422 --> 15:26.325
Peter and the fellas think that
you and I only hang out together

15:26.361 --> 15:27.929
because we're both black.

15:27.964 --> 15:29.197
Uh-huh.

15:29.232 --> 15:30.867
But I told them
that's insulting.

15:30.903 --> 15:32.170
Why is that insulting?

15:32.205 --> 15:33.739
People like to be
with their own.

15:33.774 --> 15:35.843
I mean, you don't think I
hang out with you because

15:35.878 --> 15:38.614
of your endless stories about
working your remote control

15:38.650 --> 15:42.621
or your fat son or how you once
made a dog shake its head "no"?

15:42.657 --> 15:46.061
I manipulated the
cheeseburger what like this.

15:46.096 --> 15:47.630
You boring, man.

15:47.666 --> 15:49.266
But you're black,
so we cool.

15:49.302 --> 15:51.437
That's racist.
I'm offended.

15:51.472 --> 15:52.740
Whatever.

15:52.776 --> 15:54.410
I'll see you around,
Cleveland.

15:54.445 --> 15:58.449
Man, I guess this whole
friendship was a bad idea.

15:58.485 --> 16:01.655
Just like Goodyear's
advertising strategy.

16:01.691 --> 16:03.659
All right, we have $14 million
to play with.

16:03.695 --> 16:05.563
I say we spend it all on blimps,

16:05.599 --> 16:06.899
'cause who do we want to reach?

16:06.934 --> 16:08.635
Drivers.

16:08.670 --> 16:10.404
And where are people looking
when they're driving a car?

16:10.440 --> 16:11.941
Straight up.

16:15.950 --> 16:18.820
Squire, my chamber pot
needs emptying.

16:18.855 --> 16:20.189
What's he talking about?

16:20.224 --> 16:21.759
He's been pooping
in the waffle iron.

16:21.794 --> 16:22.860
Just plug it in
and close it.

16:22.895 --> 16:24.163
It'll burn off.

16:24.199 --> 16:25.365
Look, Chris.

16:25.400 --> 16:26.500
You know, being
homecoming king

16:26.535 --> 16:28.871
doesn't mean you can
just start acting crazy.

16:28.906 --> 16:30.708
I can do whatever I want.

16:30.744 --> 16:34.048
I've been acknowledged
by my peers as their superior.

16:34.083 --> 16:36.184
You're just jealous 'cause
you've never done anything

16:36.220 --> 16:38.122
that deserves
being elected king.

16:38.157 --> 16:39.691
Okay, you want
to know the truth?

16:39.726 --> 16:41.694
They only picked you
because they felt sorry for you.

16:41.729 --> 16:42.964
Sorry?

16:42.999 --> 16:44.566
Why would they
feel sorry for me?

16:44.602 --> 16:47.238
Well, because they all think
you're a, um, you know,

16:47.273 --> 16:51.078
"groundskeeper at a public
institution" kind of guy.

16:51.113 --> 16:52.213
A what?

16:52.249 --> 16:54.517
A dope.
An idiot. A water head.

16:54.552 --> 16:57.089
You guys don't know
what you're talking about.

16:57.124 --> 16:59.727
Tonight, when they put
that crown on my head,

16:59.762 --> 17:02.198
it's gonna be the
greatest night of my life.

17:02.233 --> 17:05.538
Even better than when
I had my first kiss.

17:29.482 --> 17:31.217
I say, we were a
little hard on Chris,

17:31.252 --> 17:32.586
but I'm glad we came.

17:32.621 --> 17:34.122
He's still my brother.

17:34.157 --> 17:35.824
Hey, look, there's
the security guard

17:35.860 --> 17:37.502
that threw me out
of the bathroom earlier.

17:37.530 --> 17:39.165
And he's here
with his wife.

17:39.200 --> 17:41.301
This is like
a date for them.

17:41.337 --> 17:43.973
Good evening,
fingerers and fingerees.

17:44.008 --> 17:45.843
Sorry,
I had a little rum in the car.

17:45.879 --> 17:48.948
Anyway, please welcome your
homecoming king, Chris Griffin.

17:52.724 --> 17:55.093
Good evening, subjects.

17:55.128 --> 17:59.100
The boys' showers shall run red
with the blood of my enemies.

17:59.135 --> 18:00.469
We believe in you!

18:00.504 --> 18:01.472
Good for you, Chris!

18:01.507 --> 18:02.673
No one clap too loud.

18:02.708 --> 18:04.510
We don't want
to frighten him.

18:04.546 --> 18:06.013
Wait a minute.

18:06.048 --> 18:07.147
And now your queen,

18:07.183 --> 18:08.951
prom night car crash victim

18:08.986 --> 18:10.822
Kathleen Fitzpatrick.

18:12.726 --> 18:13.827
Aw.

18:13.862 --> 18:15.362
We miss you, Kathleen!

18:15.398 --> 18:17.033
You're heaven's queen now!

18:17.068 --> 18:18.469
Wow, she was hot.

18:18.504 --> 18:20.639
The queen is a dead girl?

18:20.675 --> 18:22.409
What does that make me?

18:22.444 --> 18:24.546
Brian and Stewie were right.

18:24.582 --> 18:26.416
This was a pity vote.

18:26.451 --> 18:27.852
We love you, Chris!

18:27.887 --> 18:29.222
You love me?

18:29.257 --> 18:31.158
You don't even know
anything about me.

18:31.193 --> 18:34.129
You just voted for me
to make yourselves feel better.

18:36.769 --> 18:39.440
She was on PCP that night,
you idiots!

18:46.454 --> 18:48.956
Chris, I-I'm so sorry.

18:48.992 --> 18:50.125
That's okay.

18:50.160 --> 18:51.896
You guys tried
to warn me.

18:51.931 --> 18:53.598
I'm sorry I was
such a jerk.

18:53.634 --> 18:54.734
Ah, don't worry about it.

18:54.769 --> 18:55.802
Are you okay?

18:55.838 --> 18:58.641
You know what?
I am.

18:58.676 --> 19:00.076
I may not be king,

19:00.112 --> 19:02.414
but I learned
I don't need anyone's pity.

19:02.449 --> 19:03.783
That's the spirit, Chris.

19:03.818 --> 19:05.753
And, hey, you're not
the homecoming king,

19:05.788 --> 19:08.258
but you'll always
be my brother.

19:08.294 --> 19:09.560
Thanks, Stewie.

19:09.595 --> 19:11.096
It means a lot
to me to know

19:11.132 --> 19:13.935
I've always got my family
looking out for me.

19:13.970 --> 19:15.737
Oh, hey, Chris.

19:15.773 --> 19:17.508
This is Tyler.

19:17.543 --> 19:20.179
Don't make this weird now.

19:20.214 --> 19:22.617
Oh, what a gentleman.

19:30.499 --> 19:32.668
Well, Cleveland, it's good
to have you back, buddy.

19:32.704 --> 19:34.071
It's good to be back.

19:34.106 --> 19:35.474
Hanging with Jerome was fun,

19:35.509 --> 19:38.079
but my best friends are
right here in this room.

19:38.114 --> 19:40.148
Hey, to celebrate,
how about we play a little

19:40.184 --> 19:42.119
<i>old-school Double Dribble?</i>

19:42.154 --> 19:44.357
Okay, but no stupid-ass
shots from the corner,

19:44.392 --> 19:45.826
because that's a glitch
in the software and...

19:45.861 --> 19:47.060
Game on!

19:49.433 --> 19:52.404
All right, bring it up the
court, and corner three!

19:52.439 --> 19:54.575
No, no. That's what
I'm talking about!

19:54.610 --> 19:56.076
Steal.

19:56.112 --> 19:59.016
Uhp, corner three.

19:59.051 --> 20:00.052
All right, here we go.

20:00.086 --> 20:01.487
I got something cooking.

20:01.522 --> 20:03.491
Uhp, you dropped
something.

20:03.526 --> 20:05.160
Think I'll head over
in this direction.

20:05.195 --> 20:06.496
Corner three!

20:06.531 --> 20:08.098
It's a rout.
It's a blowout.

20:08.134 --> 20:09.735
It's some bullcrap.

20:09.771 --> 20:11.905
Couple nice passes
there... hey!

20:11.940 --> 20:13.275
See? Competitive ball game.

20:13.310 --> 20:14.543
What should I do?

20:14.578 --> 20:15.780
Pass and then go up?

20:15.815 --> 20:18.551
And corner three!

20:18.586 --> 20:20.421
All right, enough
of this mess.

20:20.456 --> 20:22.124
Shoot it!
Shoot it from there.

20:22.160 --> 20:23.727
The refs are lettin' 'em play.

20:23.762 --> 20:25.431
I do appreciate that.

20:25.466 --> 20:26.632
Yeah, that's what
I'm talkin' about.

20:26.667 --> 20:27.935
Now I'm playing
for reals.

20:27.970 --> 20:29.136
Yeah, you're
doing pretty good.

20:29.172 --> 20:30.439
What play
should I call now?

20:30.474 --> 20:32.276
Maybe... corner three!

20:32.311 --> 20:33.745
He's hot. He is hot.

20:33.780 --> 20:35.414
Keep feeding that guy.

20:35.450 --> 20:37.284
Hi, nice to meet you.
Can I have that?

20:37.320 --> 20:38.561
Hang out over here
for a second.

20:38.589 --> 20:40.123
Corner three!

20:40.158 --> 20:41.559
You got to get
out there, Cleveland.

20:41.594 --> 20:42.994
I'm trying.

20:43.030 --> 20:45.265
He's taking advantage
of poor technology.

20:45.301 --> 20:46.836
Oh, lot of dribbling. Swipe.

20:46.871 --> 20:48.839
Here we... aw,
I hit the wrong button.

20:48.874 --> 20:51.343
I think you all know I was
going for a corner three.

20:51.367 --> 20:57.872
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru